@startuml
' Figure 3.5 - State Machine Diagrams, Order Status and Table Status
'
' Theme follows the original figure: rounded coloured states with a bold coloured name
' over a plain description line, filled start node, bullseye terminal node, and labelled
' transitions. Arranged one machine after the other down the page rather than side by
' side, so the figure sits portrait.
'
' Sizing: once width is the binding constraint the printed point size is set by canvas
' WIDTH alone, so every state description and transition label is wrapped narrow and the
' figure is allowed to grow tall in exchange - height is free up to the 9.28in budget.
'
' Order transitions verified against OrderService.NEXT / assertLegalTransition / voidOrder;
' table transitions against TableService.openTableForOrder / markBilled / markCleaning /
' markAvailable / releaseTable / setReserved.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam defaultFontSize 22
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 26

skinparam state {
  FontSize 23
  FontStyle bold
  AttributeFontSize 19
  AttributeFontStyle plain
  BorderThickness 1.8
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #607D8B
  StartColor #212121
  EndColor #212121
}
skinparam StateFontColor #111111

title State Machine Diagrams — Order Status and Table Status

state "Order Status State Machine" as OSM {
  state "PENDING"   as OP #FFF8E1 ##[bold]E65100
  state "PREPARING" as OR #E3F2FD ##[bold]1976D2
  state "READY"     as OY #E8F5E9 ##[bold]2E7D32
  state "BILLED"    as OB #E3F2FD ##[bold]1976D2
  state "COMPLETED" as OC #B2DFDB ##[bold]00695C
  state "VOID"      as OV #FFCDD2 ##[bold]C62828

  OP : order submitted,\nKOT broadcast
  OR : cook started,\npreparingStartedAt set
  OY : all lines ready,\nwaiter notified
  OB : cart locked,\ntable marked BILLED
  OC : terminal —\ntable sent to CLEANING
  OV : terminal —\ntable released

  [*] --> OP
  OP --> OR : kitchen taps "Start"
  OR --> OY : all lines ready
  OY --> OB : cashier issues bill
  OB --> OC : payment received
  OC --> [*]

  OP --> OV : waiter voids
  OR --> OV : manager voids\n(re-verified)
}

state "Table Status State Machine" as TSM {
  state "AVAILABLE" as TA #C8E6C9 ##[bold]2E7D32
  state "OCCUPIED"  as TO #FFCDD2 ##[bold]C62828
  state "BILLED"    as TB #BBDEFB ##[bold]1976D2
  state "CLEANING"  as TC #FFF9C4 ##[bold]F9A825
  state "RESERVED"  as TR #E1BEE7 ##[bold]7B1FA2

  TA : floor plan GREEN\nonly state an order\nmay open from
  TO : floor plan RED\norder in progress
  TB : floor plan BLUE\npayment pending
  TC : floor plan YELLOW\nhousekeeping,\ncurrentOrderId cleared
  TR : advance booking

  [*] --> TA
  TA --> TO : openTableForOrder\nFOR UPDATE
  TO --> TB : order reaches BILLED
  TB --> TC : order reaches COMPLETED
  TC --> TA : table cleaned, reset
  TA --> TR : reservation booked
  TR --> TA : guest seated or\nbooking cancelled
  TO --> TA : order voided\nreleaseTable
}

OSM -[hidden]-> TSM

legend bottom
  PENDING → PREPARING → READY → BILLED → COMPLETED is the
  only forward path; assertLegalTransition rejects any other
  target. VOID is a terminal side branch reachable only from
  PENDING or PREPARING — once the kitchen marks an order
  READY the dish has been committed and must be billed.
  A table can only be opened for an order from AVAILABLE,
  so a RESERVED table returns to AVAILABLE first.
endlegend

@enduml
